  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Even bridges from pair words: ℓ-pair words, untwisting limit, the z₂ = z₃ constraint, Q-form\n\n**Question (task 2026-10-12, after `pair-group-rotation.wb`).** The pair word K_κ (X₁ = t₁(θ_F), X₂ = t₂(θ_F+h), X₃ = t̂₃(θ_F+h) at pair 1) rotates pair 1 of ⟨W_a^L| by ρ_pair(1 − κΛ) exactly (ABJM point, Λ = diag(z₁, y, y, z₄)). (1) Is there an ℓ-pair word (2603's loc3 analogue) rotating the first ℓ pairs with a common κ? (2) The even-bridge family C_M through the untwisting limit at L = 3. (3) Direction independence and whether z₂ = z₃ can be relaxed. (4) Q-form of the per-pair factor. (5) The tree-level formula as it stands.\n\n> **Status.** Written by an agent while the Wolfram Engine licence is expired / the shared kernel is dead. **No code cell has been run.** Every result in the markdown cells below a code cell comes from the python port in `checks/session-2026-10-12/lpairs/` (copied from the session scratchpad `…/scratchpad/lpairs/`): **[exact]** = identity checked exactly modulo the prime P = 268435399 (all inputs rational; false-positive probability ~10⁻⁸ per entry), **[f64]** = complex128 numerics. The engine `eng.py` was validated exactly against `pgbase.py` (fused t₁, t₂, t₃, hat-t₃, 2 pairs). The Wolfram cells are a port of that code (symbols prefixed `eb`); rerun top to bottom after renewing the licence (§1 exact cells: minutes; §1e L = 4 exact: slow; §2–§3 numerics: tens of minutes; §4: minutes).\n\n**Conventions** (README; `pair-group-rotation.wb`). Chain A F A F …, site 1 leftmost, bras are rows (ψ·t). ℒ_s(u) = (u−θ_s) + hΣe_ij⊗ρ_s(E_ij), ρ_A(E_ij) = e_ij, ρ_F(E_ij) = −e_ji; fused t_k with θ̃_F = θ + (k−1)h, prefactors g_A = ∏_{j=1}^{k−1}(u−θ−jh), g_F = ∏_{j=0}^{k−2}(u−θ−jh); t̂ = exactly vanishing scalar factors dropped. ABJM point θ_{A,n} = θ_{F,n} + 2h, pair-preserving but **distinct** θ_{F,n} for the exact checks: h = 1/2, θ_F = (−3/5, −11/8, −7/9, 5/6), z = (3/2, 5/4, 5/4, 4/7), a = 1/3. W_b = (e₁ + b e₄)⊗(e₄ − b e₁) = u₀ + b u₁ + b² u₂ (u₀ = e₁e₄, u₁ = e₄e₄ − e₁e₁, u₂ = −e₄e₁). Pair word of pair p: K^(p)_κ = s² + κs[X₁/(h²λ₁) + X₂/(2h⁴yλ₂) + X₃/(6h⁵y²λ₃)] + κ²X₃X₁/(24h⁷y²λ₁λ₃), s = 1 − κ(z₁+z₄), X's at θ_{F,p}, λ_k = ∏_{n≠p}∏_{j<k}(u−θ_{A,n}−jh)·(u−θ_{F,n}−kh)∏_{j≤k−2}(u−θ_{F,n}−jh) (vanishing factors dropped). a′ = a(1−κz₄)/(1−κz₁), r := z₁/z₄.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
