       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[24]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{check (L = 3 pairs, exact)} & \\text{result}\\\\\\hline\\text{t2(u0) = t1(u0) t1(thF) on a random product bra} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{t3(u0) = 0 (full, with prefactor)} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = 3/10: <W\\_a\\^{}3|K\\^{}(1) = (1-k z1)\\^{}2 <W\\_a' W\\_a W\\_a|} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = 3/10: pairs changed by K\\^{}(2) on <W\\_a\\^{}3|} & \\left\\{1,2\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = 3/10: pairs changed by K\\^{}(3) on <W\\_a\\^{}3|} & \\left\\{1,2,3\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = -7/5: <W\\_a\\^{}3|K\\^{}(1) = (1-k z1)\\^{}2 <W\\_a' W\\_a W\\_a|} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = -7/5: pairs changed by K\\^{}(2) on <W\\_a\\^{}3|} & \\left\\{1,2\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = -7/5: pairs changed by K\\^{}(3) on <W\\_a\\^{}3|} & \\left\\{1,2,3\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = 7/4: <W\\_a\\^{}3|K\\^{}(1) = (1-k z1)\\^{}2 <W\\_a' W\\_a W\\_a|} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = 7/4: pairs changed by K\\^{}(2) on <W\\_a\\^{}3|} & \\left\\{1,2\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{kappa = 7/4: pairs changed by K\\^{}(3) on <W\\_a\\^{}3|} & \\left\\{1,2,3\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "fd595b8a-37af-462c-9e0e-28e6ffd704e7"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python results [exact]** (`task1a.py`, `task1b.py`; L = 2 and 3, distinct and fully periodic θ_F).\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| t₂(u₀) = t₁(u₀)·t₁(θ_F) (operator identity, random bra) | True (L = 2, 3) |\n| t₃(u₀) = 0 (full) | True |\n| ⟨W_a^L\\|K^(1)_κ = (1−κz₁)²⟨W_a′⊗W_a^{L−1}\\|, κ ∈ {3/10, −7/5, 1/z₄} | True (L = 2, 3) |\n| pairs changed by K^(2) / K^(3) on ⟨W_a^3\\| | {1, 2} / {1, 2, 3} — also for each single word X₁, X₂, X₃, X₃X₁ of pair p |\n\nSo a pair-p word does **not** localise on pair p: it is block-localised on pairs 1…p (2603's eq. `localized`: ⟨𝒲^L\\|∏_{k≤ℓ}t̂(θ_k) lives on the first ℓ sites). With fully periodic θ the pair-p words *are* the pair-1 words (same operators). The naive product ∏_{p≤ℓ}K^(p)_κ fails (§1b).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 1b. Naive products and the span of the 5^ℓ multilinear monomials (exact)\n\nMonomials ∏_{p≤ℓ} w_p, w_p ∈ {1, X₁, X₂, X₃, X₃X₁}^(p). The target ⟨W_a′^ℓ⊗W_a^{L−ℓ}\\| is unique, so if any combination of monomials produced it, the rank test would show it.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ebT1b = Flatten[Table[Module[{ch = ebChain[Take[ebthF, lp], ebz], ref, mons},\n     ref = ebWstate[ConstantArray[eba, lp]]; mons = ebMonos[ch, ref, l];\n     Table[With[{ap = eba (1 - kap ebz[[4]])/(1 - kap ebz[[1]])},\n       With[{tgt = ebWstate[Join[ConstantArray[ap, l], ConstantArray[eba, lp - l]]], naive = Fold[ebApplyK[ch, #1, #2, kap, eby] &, ref, Range[l]]},\n        {lp, l, kap, naive == (1 - kap ebz[[1]])^(2 l) tgt, MatrixRank[mons], MatrixRank[Append[mons, tgt]]}]], {kap, {3/10, 1/ebz[[4]]}}]],\n    {lp, 2, 3}, {l, 2, lp}], 2];\nGrid[Prepend[ebT1b, {\"L\", \"l\", \"kappa\", \"naive prod_p K^(p) works\", \"rank(monomials)\", \"rank(monomials + target)\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
