      {
       "data": "Out[29]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{all 25 multilinear monomials block-localise: <W\\_a\\^{}3|m = lambda\\_m (<W\\_a\\^{}2|m on 2 pairs) (x) W\\_a} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\text{dim of span(monomials) intersected with span\\{u\\_i (x) u\\_j\\} (x) W\\_a} & 5\\\\\\hline\\text{intersection basis (coefficients of u\\_i (x) u\\_j, i, j = 0, 1, 2)} & \\begin{matrix}\\left\\{-\\frac{576}{49},-\\frac{192}{49},0,-\\frac{72}{7},-\\frac{24}{7},0,0,0,1\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{0,\\frac{64}{49},0,0,\\frac{8}{7},0,0,1,0\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{\\frac{64}{49},0,0,\\frac{8}{7},0,0,1,0,0\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{0,0,0,9,3,1,0,0,0\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{9,3,1,0,0,0,0,0,0\\right\\}\\end{matrix}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "19bf48e7-1805-4cee-9c1f-7ec6eb1d9511"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python results [exact]** (`task1e.py`, `task1f.py`, `task1j.py`).\n\n- **Block localisation** holds for all 25 multilinear monomials (λ_m = product of single-word λ's); the same-pair squares X₁², X₁X₂, X₂², X₂X₃, X₃² do **not** block-localise. So the ℓ-pair problem reduces exactly to the ℓ-pair chain with 5^ℓ monomials, as in 2603 — and there the target is absent (§1b).\n- **W-type states in the span: dimension 5**, = span{u_i}⊗W_a ⊕ W_{ar}⊗span{u_j} (r = z₁/z₄; for a = 1/3 the second family has coefficients (64/49, 8/7, 1) = W_{7/8}, 7/8 = a·21/8; for a = −1 it is W_{−21/8}). The same 5-dim space appears with per-pair degree ≤ 2 (100 monomials). **No W_b⊗W_c with b ∉ {a, ar} and c ≠ a**: pair 1 can be rotated freely only with pair 2 untouched; pair 2 can be rotated freely only if pair 1 carries the **fixed** inverse twist a → a z₁/z₄.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 1d. The structure: pretwisted pair words, the chain word, right-end words (L = 3, exact)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ebT1d = Module[{ch = ebChain[Take[ebthF, 3], ebz], r = ebz[[1]]/ebz[[4]], rows = {}},\n   Do[Module[{uF = ch[\"th\"][[2 p]], pre, x31, c},\n     pre = ebWstate[Join[ConstantArray[eba r, p - 1], ConstantArray[eba, 4 - p]]];\n     x31 = ebApplyT[1, uF, ebApplyT[3, uF + ebh, pre, ch, True], ch];\n     c = 24 ebh^7 eby^2 ebLam[ch, 1, uF, p] ebLam[ch, 3, uF + ebh, p] ebz[[4]]^2;\n     AppendTo[rows, {\"p = \" <> ToString[p] <> \": (X3X1)^(p) <W_ar^(p-1) W_a^(L-p+1)| = c <W_ar^p W_a^(L-p)|\", x31 == c ebWstate[Join[ConstantArray[eba r, p], ConstantArray[eba, 3 - p]]]}];\n     Do[With[{ap = eba (1 - kap ebz[[4]])/(1 - kap ebz[[1]])},\n       AppendTo[rows, {\"p = \" <> ToString[p] <> \", kappa = \" <> ToString[kap, InputForm] <> \": K^(p) on <W_ar^(p-1) W_a^(L-p+1)| rotates pair p\",\n         ebApplyK[ch, pre, p, kap, eby] == (1 - kap ebz[[1]])^2 ebWstate[Join[ConstantArray[eba r, p - 1], {ap}, ConstantArray[eba, 3 - p]]]}]], {kap, {3/10, 1/ebz[[4]]}}]], {p, 1, 3}];\n   rows];\nebT1e = Module[{ch = ebChain[Take[ebthF, 3], ebz], ref = ebWstate[{eba, eba, eba}], tA, y1, y2, y3},\n   tA = ch[\"th\"][[5]];\n   y1 = ebApplyT[1, tA, #, ch] &; y2 = ebApplyT[2, tA, #, ch] &; y3 = ebApplyT[3, tA + ebh, #, ch, True] &;\n   {{\"Y1\", ebChanged[y1[ref], {eba, eba, eba}]}, {\"Y2\", ebChanged[y2[ref], {eba, eba, eba}]}, {\"Y3\", ebChanged[y3[ref], {eba, eba, eba}]},\n    {\"Y1 Y3\", ebChanged[y1[y3[ref]], {eba, eba, eba}]}, {\"Y1 Y1\", ebChanged[y1[y1[ref]], {eba, eba, eba}]}}];\nColumn[{Grid[ebT1d, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left], Grid[Prepend[ebT1e, {\"right-end word (Y1 = t1(thA_L), Y2 = t2(thA_L), Y3 = t3^(thA_L + h))\", \"pairs changed\"}], Frame -> All]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
