  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python results [f64]** (`task2.py`; python state numbers are 0-based, Wolfram rows 1-based). Overlap of the matched twisted state with Ψ₀ = 1.000000 for all 26 states at ε = 10⁻⁴ (sector gaps ≥ 0.038). Finite-twist exactness: max \\|RHS − LHS\\| = 4·10⁻⁷ (F1, F2), 1.3·10⁻⁶ (F3, F4), 2·10⁻¹⁶ (G) (cancellation K/N ~ 10⁸ against ⟨W\\|Ψ⟩ ~ 10⁻¹⁰). \\|RHS − target\\| at ε = 10⁻²/10⁻³/10⁻⁴:\n\n| # | Dynkin | E | C₄ = C₂ (data) | F1 → C₄ | F4 → C₄ | F2 → C₂ | F3 → C₂ | G → C₀ = 0 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | [3,0,3] | 0 | 1 | 4e-12 / 2e-10 / 1e-7 | 3e-13 / 8e-11 / 2e-8 | 4e-12 / 6e-10 / 4e-8 | 3e-13 / 8e-11 / 2e-8 | 1e-16 (C₀ = 1) |\n| 16 | [1,0,1] | 10.343 | −0.171126 | 6.0e-3 / 6.0e-4 / 6.1e-5 | 1.5e-3 / 1.5e-4 / 1.5e-5 | 3.8e-3 / 3.8e-4 / 3.8e-5 | 1.5e-3 / 1.5e-4 / 1.5e-5 | 3.3e-5 / 3.3e-7 / 3.3e-9 |\n| 17 | [1,0,1] | 21.657 | −0.027138 | 1.4e-3 / 1.4e-4 / 1.4e-5 | 6.9e-4 / 6.9e-5 / 6.9e-6 | 1.0e-3 / 1.1e-4 / 1.0e-5 | 6.9e-4 / 6.9e-5 / 6.9e-6 | 2.4e-6 / 2.5e-8 / 2.5e-10 |\n| 18 | [1,0,1] | 23.544 | −0.035872 − 0.028637i | 2.5e-3 / 2.5e-4 / 2.5e-5 | 1.3e-3 / 1.3e-4 / 1.3e-5 | 1.9e-3 / 1.9e-4 / 1.9e-5 | 1.3e-3 / 1.3e-4 / 1.3e-5 | 2.1e-6 / 2.2e-8 / 2.2e-10 |\n| 19 | [1,0,1] | 23.544 | −0.035872 + 0.028637i | same as 18 | | | | |\n| 20 | [1,0,1] | 6.456 | 0.129924 − 0.081713i | 4.5e-3 / 4.5e-4 / 4.5e-5 | 4.9e-4 / 4.7e-5 / 4.8e-6 | 2.5e-3 / 2.5e-4 / 2.5e-5 | 4.9e-4 / 4.7e-5 / 4.8e-6 | 5.9e-5 / 5.9e-7 / 5.9e-9 |\n| 21 | [1,0,1] | 6.456 | 0.129924 + 0.081713i | same as 20 | | | | |\n\nThe other 19 states (targets 0: [4,0,0], [1,2,1]², [2,0,2]³, [2,1,0]³, [0,0,4], [0,1,2]³, [0,2,0]², singlets⁴) → 0: max \\|RHS\\| at ε = 10⁻⁴ is 2.5·10⁻⁵ (F1), 1·10⁻⁵ (F2), 3·10⁻⁵ (F3, F4), 4·10⁻⁵ (G); exactly 0 where ⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ⟩ = 0 by weight. **All families converge as O(ε) to the data**, so C₁ = C₂ (M = 1, 2) at L = 3 are given by the one-pair word through both HW shifts; M = 3 (global) is consistent (C₀ = 0 except the vacuum).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Rerun 2026-10-13 (Wolfram, L = 3, 7.5 min).** Reproduced: overlap of the matched twisted state with $\\Psi_0\\to1$; all families converge as $O(\\varepsilon)$ to the data (states 1, 17-22; $|{\\rm RHS}-C|$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-2},10^{-3},10^{-4}$: state 17 F4 1.5e-3 / 1.5e-4 / 1.5e-5, F3 1.5e-3 / 1.5e-4 / 1.5e-5, as in the table). G column is $O(\\varepsilon^2)$ small.\n\n**DISCREPANCY (2026-10-13 rerun), labelling only.** The F1 and F2 columns of the python table are **swapped** relative to the family definitions above. Python `task2.py` builds F1 with `sgn = -1`, i.e. $\\kappa=1/(z_1+a(z_1-z_4))$ ($a'-a=+1$), and F2 with $\\kappa=1/(z_1-a(z_1-z_4))$ ($a'-a=-1$), although its header comment (and this notebook) define F1 with $a'-a=-1$. The Wolfram cell follows the documented definitions, so its F1/F2 columns are the python F2/F1 columns: state 17 (python #16): F1 3.75e-3 / 3.77e-4 / 3.74e-5 here vs python F2 3.8e-3 / 3.8e-4 / 3.8e-5; F2 5.98e-3 / 6.04e-4 / 6.0e-5 here vs python F1 6.0e-3 / 6.0e-4 / 6.1e-5; the same swap for states 18-22. The G column differs for the same reason (G uses the F1 $\\kappa$; python used its own F1, the opposite sign): state 17 G = 8.2e-6 / 8.3e-8 / 8.3e-10 here vs 3.3e-5 / 3.3e-7 / 3.3e-9 in python. Both choices converge to the same $C_M$ because $C_2=C_4$ on all these states, so this test cannot discriminate between $a'-a=\\pm1$; the physics claim is unaffected, but the table's F1/F2 labels should be read as swapped.\n\n(fixed 2026-10-13: cell 20 imported the whole `abjm-hw-states.wxf` (the L4 key is 3 GB in memory); it now reads `checks/session-2026-10-13/epsexp/hw_L3.json` (`RawJSON`, L3 states, same 26 states in the same order). Cell 20 also memoises `ebSectorMatrix` (speed; without it the cell took more than 10 min).)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Direction independence; is z₂ = z₃ needed?\n\n(a) **Linear prescription** κ = 1 − cε exactly. From a′ − a = aκ(z₁−z₄)/(1−κz₁) → a(φ₁−φ₄)/(c−φ₁) at leading order, a′ − a → −1 requires **a = (φ₁ − c)/(φ₁ − φ₄)** (M = 1, target C₄). Three directions with φ₂ = φ₃ and two c. (b) **z₂ ≠ z₃ at finite twist**: residual of the best word vs d = z₂ − z₃. (c) **Limit with z₂ − z₃ = 0.5 ε^q**, q = 1, 2, 3 (q = 1: a direction with φ₂ ≠ φ₃), word K_A (y → (z₂+z₃)/2 in the X₂ term, y² → z₂z₃ in the X₃, X₃X₁ terms).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ebSt3 = {1, 5, 17, 18, 19, 21, 23, 26};\nebRun3a = Flatten[Table[Module[{ch = ebNumChain[eps, phi, ebThdir], st},\n      st = ebTwisted[ch, ebSt3];\n      Table[Module[{psi = st[i][[1]], sec = st[i][[3]], taus, z = ch[\"z\"]},\n        taus = ebTaus[ch, psi, sec];\n        Table[With[{a = (phi[[1]] - c)/(phi[[1]] - phi[[4]]), kap = 1 - c eps},\n          {phi, c, eps, i, Abs[ebKval[ch, taus, kap, z[[2]]] (ebWstate[{a, a, a}] . psi)/(1 - kap z[[1]])^2 - ebHW[[i]][\"C\"][[5]]]}], {c, {0.3, 2.0}}]], {i, ebSt3}]],\n     {phi, {{0.9, 0.35, 0.35, -1.1}, {-0.7, 1.3, 1.3, 0.4}, {1.5, -0.6, -0.6, 0.2}}}, {eps, {10.^-2, 10.^-3, 10.^-4}}], 3];\n(* (b) finite twist, z2 != z3: relative residual of K_A and of the least-squares best word *)\nebRun3b = Table[Module[{z = {1.5, 1.25 + d/2, 1.25 - d/2, 4/7.}, ch, ref, xs, kap = 0.3, s, l1, l2, l3, uF, tgt, kA, mat},\n    ch = ebChain[{-0.6, -1.375, -7/9.}, z, 0.5]; uF = ch[\"th\"][[2]];\n    ref = ebWstate[{1/3., 1/3., 1/3.}]; xs = ebXs[ch, ref, 1];\n    l1 = ebLam[ch, 1, uF, 1]; l2 = ebLam[ch, 2, uF + 0.5, 1]; l3 = ebLam[ch, 3, uF + 0.5, 1]; s = 1 - kap (z[[1]] + z[[4]]);\n    tgt = (1 - kap z[[1]])^2 ebWstate[{(1/3.) (1 - kap z[[4]])/(1 - kap z[[1]]), 1/3., 1/3.}];\n    kA = s^2 ref + kap s (xs[[1]]/(0.5^2 l1) + xs[[2]]/(2 0.5^4 ((z[[2]] + z[[3]])/2) l2) + xs[[3]]/(6 0.5^5 z[[2]] z[[3]] l3)) + kap^2 xs[[4]]/(24 0.5^7 z[[2]] z[[3]] l1 l3);\n    mat = Transpose[Prepend[xs, ref]];\n    {d, Norm[kA - tgt]/Norm[tgt], Norm[mat . LeastSquares[mat, tgt] - tgt]/Norm[tgt]}], {d, {10.^-1, 10.^-2, 10.^-3, 10.^-4}}];\nColumn[{Grid[Prepend[ebRun3a, {\"phi\", \"c\", \"eps\", \"state #\", \"|RHS - C4|\"}], Frame -> All], Grid[Prepend[ebRun3b, {\"z2 - z3\", \"rel. residual K_A\", \"least-squares best\"}], Frame -> All]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
