  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python results [f64]** (`task3a.py`, `task3b.py`, `task3c.py`).\n\n(a) All six (φ, c) runs converge O(ε) to the same data value C₄; \\|RHS − LHS\\| ≤ 2·10⁻⁶ throughout. State 16 ([1,0,1], C₄ = −0.171126), \\|RHS − C₄\\| at ε = 10⁻²/10⁻³/10⁻⁴:\n\n| φ | c = 0.3 | c = 2.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| (0.9, 0.35, 0.35, −1.1) | 3.4e-3 / 3.4e-4 / 3.4e-5 (a = 0.300) | 1.8e-2 / 1.9e-3 / 1.9e-4 (a = −0.550) |\n| (−0.7, 1.3, 1.3, 0.4) | 3.4e-3 / 3.4e-4 / 3.4e-5 (a = 0.909) | 1.1e-2 / 1.1e-3 / 1.1e-4 (a = 2.455) |\n| (1.5, −0.6, −0.6, 0.2) | 1.8e-3 / 1.8e-4 / 1.8e-5 (a = 0.923) | 2.9e-2 / 3.2e-3 / 3.2e-4 (a = −0.385) |\n\nSame pattern for states 17, 18, 20 (targets −0.027138, −0.035872 − 0.028637i, 0.129924 − 0.081713i), the vacuum (→ 1, ≤ 3·10⁻⁷) and the zero-target states 4, 22, 25 (≤ 4·10⁻⁵ at ε = 10⁻⁴). **The limit is independent of the direction φ and of c.**\n\n(b) Finite twist, L = 3, κ = 3/10 (κ = 7/4 in brackets): relative residual for d = z₂ − z₃ = 10⁻¹, 10⁻², 10⁻³, 10⁻⁴: K_A 5.25e-3, 5.25e-4, 5.25e-5, 5.25e-6 (3.05e-2 … 3.05e-5); least-squares best word 5.19e-3, 5.25e-4, 5.25e-5, 5.25e-6 (3.01e-2 …); K with y = z₂: ≈ 6× worse. **Obstruction linear in z₂ − z₃, and K_A is already optimal** — z₂ = z₃ is a genuine requirement for exactness at finite twist.\n\n(c) Limit with z₂ − z₃ = 0.5ε^q (F1 → C₄, F3 → C₂): the finite-twist identity fails only by \\|RHS − LHS\\| ≈ 0.1(z₂−z₃)²/ε (state 4 [2,0,2]: 2.6e-4 / 2.7e-5 / 2.7e-6 for q = 1; 2.6e-8 / 2.7e-11 for q = 2; the [1,0,1] states and singlets stay at the noise level ≤ 8·10⁻⁷), and **\\|RHS − target\\| is identical to the z₂ = z₃ runs** (state 16: 3.8e-3 / 3.8e-4 / 3.8e-5 for every q in F1; 1.5e-3 / 1.5e-4 / 1.5e-5 in F3). **So the regulator needs z₂ = z₃ only up to O(ε): any direction φ (φ₂ ≠ φ₃ allowed) gives the same limit**; a splitting z₂ − z₃ ≫ √ε would spoil it.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Q-form of the per-pair factor (ABJM point)\n\nGauge of `sov-Q-dictionary-L4.wb` (shift convention Q(u−h)): Σ_{a=0}^4(−1)^aτ_a(u)Q(u−ah) = 0, Q_i(u) = z_i^{u/h}Φ(u)q_i(u), Φ(u) = V₄(u)Φ(u−h), V₄(u) = ∏_A(u−θ_A)∏_F(u−θ_F−h), q_i polynomial. Pair 1, u₀ = θ_F + h = θ_A − h. \"rest\" = product over the **other** pairs; F₃(u) = ∏_F(u−θ_F)(u−θ_F−h); P_I(u) = det[z_i^{2−s}q_i(u−sh)]_{i∈I, s=0,1,2}; q_I = P_I/F₃ (polynomial: reduced Casoratian = dual Q); Z_I = ∏_{i∈I}z_i.\n\n- τ_F := τ₁(θ_F) = Q_j(θ_F)/Q_j(θ_F−h) = z_jV₄(θ_F)q_j(θ_F)/q_j(θ_F−h)  (**any j**: two-term Baxter at θ_F)\n- x := τ₁(u₀) = [V₄^rest(u₀)/F₃^rest(θ_F)]·Z_I⁴·det[z_i⁻¹q_i(θ_F+h), z_i⁻³q_i(θ_F−h), z_i⁻⁴q_i(θ_F−2h)] / q_I(θ_F)\n- τ₂(u₀) = x·τ_F (operator identity); Q-form: same prefactor × V₄(θ_F) with columns (z⁻¹q(θ_F+h), z⁻²q(θ_F), z⁻⁴q(θ_F−2h))\n- τ̂₃(u₀) = h·V₄^rest(u₀)V₄(θ_F)V₄(θ_F−h)·Z_I·[F₃^rest(u₀)/F₃^rest(θ_F)]·q_I(θ_F+h)/q_I(θ_F)  (**any triple I**)\n\nDerivation: θ_A = θ_F + 2h + δ, δ → 0 in the generic A-site Cramer formulas τ_a(θ_A−h) = D_a/D₀ (D_a = det_{i∈I, j∈{1..4}∖{a+1}}Q_i(θ_A−jh)); the zeros of D₀ (F₃ at θ_F) and of V₄(θ_A−h) are vacuum factors and cancel explicitly; τ₃(θ_A−h)/δ → τ₃′(u₀) = τ̂₃(u₀). So **X₁ ↔ single Q ratio (F site), X₃ ↔ single dual-Q ratio q_I(θ_F+h)/q_I(θ_F) (A site of the pair), X₂ = x·X₁ with x a gapped Casoratian over the reduced Casoratian.** The per-pair factor:\n\nK_κ = s² + κs[τ_F/(h²λ₁) + xτ_F/(2h⁴yλ₂) + τ̂₃/(6h⁵y²λ₃)] + κ²τ̂₃τ_F/(24h⁷y²λ₁λ₃).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ebQch = ebChain[{-0.6, -1.375}, {1.5, 1.25, 2/3, 4/7}, 0.5];\nebFull[ch_, k_, u_, reg_: False] := ebApplyT[k, u, IdentityMatrix[256] + 0. I, ch, reg];   (* m[[p,q]] = (e_p . t)_q *)\n{ebQev, ebQV} = Eigensystem[ebFull[ebQch, 1, 0.37] + 0.61 ebFull[ebQch, 3, -0.29, True] + 0.23 ebFull[ebQch, 2, 0.83]];\nebTauAll[k_, u_, reg_: False] := With[{m = ebFull[ebQch, k, u, reg]}, Map[(Conjugate[#] . (m . #))/(Conjugate[#] . #) &, ebQV]];\nebUs = Subdivide[-2.3, 2.1, 29] + 0.0123;\nebTauTab = Table[If[k == 0, ConstantArray[1., {30, 256}], Table[ebTauAll[k, u], {u, ebUs}]], {k, 0, 4}];   (* [[k+1, point, state]] *)\nebV4[ch_, u_] := Times @@ MapThread[If[#1 == \"A\", u - #2, u - #2 - ch[\"h\"]] &, {ch[\"types\"], ch[\"th\"]}];\n(* fixed 2026-10-13: rows that are exactly zero (3 of the 256 states at degree 0) gave 0/0; as in the python (sc[sc == 0] = 1) they are now left unscaled *)\nebSolveQ[ch_, s_, zi_, maxdeg_: 8] := Module[{h = ch[\"h\"], rows, svd, sv},\n   Catch[Do[rows = Table[Sum[(-1)^a zi^(-a) ebTauTab[[a + 1, m, s]] Product[ebV4[ch, ebUs[[m]] - b h], {b, a, 3}] (ebUs[[m]] - a h)^Range[0, deg], {a, 0, 4}], {m, Length[ebUs]}];\n     rows = #/If[Max[Abs[#]] == 0, 1, Max[Abs[#]]] & /@ rows; svd = SingularValueDecomposition[rows]; sv = Diagonal[svd[[2]]];\n     If[Last[sv]/First[sv] < 10^-9, Throw[svd[[3]][[All, -1]]/Last[svd[[3]][[All, -1]]]]], {deg, 0, maxdeg}]; $Failed]];\nebQForm[ch_, qs_, i3_] := Module[{h = ch[\"h\"], z = ch[\"z\"], thF = ch[\"th\"][[2]], u0, q, v4r, f3r, pI, dfit, pts, cI, qI, zI, dd, pref},\n   u0 = thF + h; q[i_, u_] := qs[[i]] . u^Range[0, Length[qs[[i]]] - 1];\n   v4r[u_] := Times @@ Table[If[ch[\"types\"][[s]] == \"A\", u - ch[\"th\"][[s]], u - ch[\"th\"][[s]] - h], {s, 3, Length[ch[\"th\"]]}];\n   f3r[u_] := Times @@ Table[(u - ch[\"th\"][[s]]) (u - ch[\"th\"][[s]] - h), {s, 4, Length[ch[\"th\"]], 2}];\n   pI[u_] := Det[Table[z[[i]]^(2 - sh) q[i, u - sh h], {i, i3}, {sh, 0, 2}]];\n   dfit = Max[Total[(Length[qs[[#]]] - 1) & /@ i3] - Length[ch[\"th\"]], 0];\n   pts = Subdivide[-2.7, 2.9, 39] + 0.031;\n   cI = LeastSquares[Table[x^j, {x, pts}, {j, 0, dfit}], Table[pI[x]/Times @@ Table[(x - ch[\"th\"][[s]]) (x - ch[\"th\"][[s]] - h), {s, 2, Length[ch[\"th\"]], 2}], {x, pts}]];\n   qI[u_] := cI . u^Range[0, dfit]; zI = Times @@ z[[i3]];\n   dd[cols_] := Det[Table[z[[i]]^(-j) q[i, ch[\"th\"][[1]] - j h], {i, i3}, {j, cols}]];\n   pref = v4r[u0]/f3r[thF] zI^4/qI[thF];\n   <|\"tauF\" -> Table[z[[j]] ebV4[ch, thF] q[j, thF]/q[j, thF - h], {j, 4}], \"x\" -> pref dd[{1, 3, 4}], \"tau2\" -> pref ebV4[ch, thF] dd[{1, 2, 4}],\n    \"tau3hat\" -> h v4r[u0] ebV4[ch, thF] ebV4[ch, thF - h] zI f3r[u0]/f3r[thF] qI[u0]/qI[thF]|>];\n(* fixed 2026-10-13: the Max[...] around the first term (tau_F over the four j) was not closed; the four deviations are now a list *)\nebQchk = Module[{uF = -0.6, tF, x, t2, t3, dev = {0, 0, 0, 0}},\n   tF = ebTauAll[1, uF]; x = ebTauAll[1, uF + 0.5]; t2 = ebTauAll[2, uF + 0.5]; t3 = ebTauAll[3, uF + 0.5, True];\n   Do[Module[{qs = Table[ebSolveQ[ebQch, s, ebQch[\"z\"][[i]]], {i, 4}]},\n     Do[With[{f = ebQForm[ebQch, qs, i3]},\n       dev = MapThread[Max, {dev, {Max[Abs[f[\"tauF\"] - tF[[s]]]/Abs[tF[[s]]]], Abs[f[\"x\"] - x[[s]]]/Abs[x[[s]]], Abs[f[\"tau2\"] - t2[[s]]]/Abs[t2[[s]]], Abs[f[\"tau3hat\"] - t3[[s]]]/Abs[t3[[s]]]}}]], {i3, {{1, 2, 3}, {2, 3, 4}, {1, 2, 4}, {1, 3, 4}}}]], {s, 256}];\n   dev];\nGrid[Transpose[{{\"tau_F\", \"x = tau1(u0)\", \"tau2(u0)\", \"tau3^(u0)\"}, ebQchk}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
