  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Python results [f64]** (`qf.py`, `qdict.py`, `task4a–d.py`).\n\n- L = 2, ABJM point, generic twist z = (3/2, 5/4, 2/3, 4/7): joint spectrum simple (min gap 8·10⁻⁶), all 1024 Baxter solutions found (degree patterns e.g. (2,2,2,2) ×28, (3,1,2,2) ×12, …). Max relative deviation of the four Q-formulas over **256 states × 4 triples**: τ_F 5.6·10⁻¹², x 3.3·10⁻⁸, τ₂(u₀) 3.3·10⁻⁸, τ̂₃(u₀) 3.5·10⁻⁸; identity τ₂(u₀) = xτ_F: 4.4·10⁻¹³.\n- L = 3 (formulas with \"rest\" = pairs 2, 3), sectors (2,0,0,−2) [24 states] and (2,1,−1,−2) [9 states]: max deviations 3.7·10⁻¹², 9.4·10⁻⁷, 9.4·10⁻⁷, 1.1·10⁻⁶ and 9·10⁻¹³, 2·10⁻⁸, 2·10⁻⁸, 2.4·10⁻⁸ (Baxter-conditioning limited).\n- Near the ABJM point (θ_A = θ_F + 2h + δ, generic twist, L = 2): τ₁(θ_A−h) = −0.45551, −0.43264, −0.43039 for δ = 10⁻², 10⁻³, 10⁻⁴ → x = −0.43014 at δ = 0; τ₃(θ_A−h)/δ = 0.004472, 0.004562, 0.004570 → τ̂₃(u₀) = 0.004571 (linear convergence; first state shown).\n- **Factorisation.** With S = z₁ + z₄, Σ = 2x₁ − x₂/y + 2x₃/y², Π = x₃x₁/y² (normalised eigenvalues): K(κ) = 1 − κ(2S − Σ) + κ²(S² − SΣ + Π) = (1 − κρ₁)(1 − κρ₂), ρ = S − r, r² − Σr + Π = 0 (vacuum: ρ₁ = ρ₂ = z₁). It does **not** factor rationally: at L = 2, z₂ = z₃, 53 of the 256 states (all with real τ's) have complex ρ₁,₂. At κ = 1/z₄: K = (z₁² − z₁Σ + Π)/z₄² (previous session).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Rerun 2026-10-13 (Wolfram, L = 2, 256 states, 75 s).** Max relative deviation of the four Q-formulas over 256 states x 4 triples: $\\tau_F$ 1.4e-11, $x$ 4.0e-8, $\\tau_2(u_0)$ 3.5e-8, $\\hat\\tau_3(u_0)$ 3.4e-8 (python: 5.6e-12, 3.3e-8, 3.3e-8, 3.5e-8): reproduced to the same order (Baxter-conditioning limited; `Det::luc` warnings appear for badly conditioned $3\\times3$ determinants).\n\n(fixed 2026-10-13: two port bugs in this cell. (1) `ebQchk` had an unclosed `Max[` around the first deviation term (syntax error `ToExpression::sntx`); the four deviations are now a list as intended. (2) `ebSolveQ` divided exactly-zero rows by their max (0/0, `Power::infy`) for 3 of the 256 states (28, 123, 159) at degree 0; the python guard `sc[sc == 0] = 1` is now applied. The L = 3 Q-form check of the python (sectors (2,0,0,-2) and (2,1,-1,-2)) and the near-ABJM $\\delta\\to0$ check are not in this notebook and were not rerun.)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Summary — the tree-level formula as it now stands\n\n**Formula.** Untwisted HW cyclic state Ψ₀ at the ABJM point; regulator z = 1 + εφ, z₂ − z₃ = O(ε) (exactly z₂ = z₃ for finite-twist exactness), pair-preserving θ_{F,n} = εϑ_n, θ_A = θ_F + 2h; Ψ_ε = twisted eigenstate continuing Ψ₀. With the pair-1 word (X's at θ_{F,1}):\n\n  ⟨W_a′⊗W_a^{L−1}\\|Ψ_ε⟩ = K_κ(τ)·⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ_ε⟩/(1−κz₁)²  [**exact**, any κ, any a; L = 2, 3 mod P, L = 4 mod P],\n\n  K_κ(τ) = s² + κs[τ_F/(h²λ₁) + xτ_F/(2h⁴yλ₂) + τ̂₃/(6h⁵y²λ₃)] + κ²τ̂₃τ_F/(24h⁷y²λ₁λ₃), s = 1 − κ(z₁+z₄),\n\nτ_F = Q_j(θ_F)/Q_j(θ_F−h), τ̂₃ ∝ q_I(θ_F+h)/q_I(θ_F) (dual Q), x = gapped Casoratian / q_I(θ_F) (§4) [f64, 256 states at L = 2, 33 at L = 3]. The note's (3.6) C_M = 𝒩₁₂₃⟨vac^{L−M}⊗W₋₁^M\\|Ψ₀⟩:\n\n| M | prescription | limit | evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | κ = 1/(z₁ − a(z₁−z₄)) (or κ = 1 − cε, a = (φ₁−c)/(φ₁−φ₄)); or κ = 1/z₄, a = +1 | lim_{ε→0} K_κ(τ)⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ_ε⟩/(1−κz₁)² = C_{M=1} | [f64] L = 3, all 26 HW states, O(ε), 3 directions × 2 c; L = 2 (previous session) |\n| L−1 | κ = 1/z₄, a = −1; or a′ − a = +1 (shift by −a′) | same expression → C_{M=L−1} | [f64] L = 3 (M = 2) |\n| L | global ρ(1−κΛ): [(1−κz₄)/(1−κz₁)]^L∏_i(1−κz_i)^{μ_i}⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ⟩ | C₀ (= 0 unless vacuum) | [f64] L = 3 |\n| 2 … L−2 | **not reachable**: no common-κ ℓ-pair word; the only multi-pair words are end-growing chains with fixed Λ⁻¹ on all but one pair | — | [exact] L = 3 (ℓ = 2, 3), L = 4 (ℓ = 2) |\n\nPlus C_M = (−1)^{L+μ₄}C_{L−M} (HW symmetry), so at L = 3 every even bridge is covered; **L = 4, M = 2 is the first open case.**\n\n**What remains.** (i) ⟨W_a^L\\|Ψ⟩ in SoV/Q form (the analogue of 2603's 𝕎_ω determinant) — the per-pair factor is now explicit in Q's but does not factor into rational linear factors in κ, so a determinant form like 2603's 𝔸_{ℓ,κ} has to be found from the full expression. (ii) The middle even bridges 2 ≤ M ≤ L−2: need a different reference or a second integrable family (left/right end words do not combine; §1d). (iii) Norms and 𝒩₁₂₃. (iv) Rerun this notebook when the licence is back.\n\nFiles: python `checks/session-2026-10-12/lpairs/` (`eng.py` engine, `lp.py` words, `modlin.py`/`modspan.py` exact mod-P linear algebra, `supp.py`, `untw.py` + `hwdata.py` + `wxf.py` untwisting, `qf.py` + `qdict.py` Q's, `task1a–k.py`, `task2.py`, `task3a–c.py`, `task4a–d.py`, `RESULTS.md`).",
